      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VRChat has always sort of had this problem where avatars are always clipping through the floor a little bit, and I've always compensated by raising the hip bone before upload.\nAfter the update, this problem worsened in 3-point but improved in 6-point. In 6-point, my avatar would now float above the floor, as if the issue was corrected and I should undo my raised hip fix.\n...but after rerunning Oculus + SteamVR room setup (hybrid FBT) to refine my height configuration (it's drifted a bit since I last did it), my feet are perfectly aligned with the floor in both modes, so now I'm not sure if it's a real issue or simply caused by less-than-perfect room calibration.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
